      "observed": "guardOwnedWindow exists only as anunref interval inside thecontrollerprocess. If theouterlauncher dies and thecontrollerexits normally beforethe next50ms poll, both theinterval and outerpost-spawncleanup disappear. A stillliveowneddescendant has no surviving owner to enforce theabsolute deadline.",
      "independentReproduction": [
        "Use the exactfrozen owned-window function in a pureNode detachedprimary with a300ms owneddeadline. Spawn anunref pureNodeintervalchild with stdioignore, preserving thesamePGID.",
        "Primary sendsREADY thennaturallyexits after15ms. Theouterlauncher exits immediatelyonREADY.",
        "At500ms (past the300ms deadline), outerPID38818 andprimaryPID38819 aredead whileownedchildPID38820 isstillalive. Thisis not merely a delayedpoll within thedeadline.",
        "The review then independentlycalls terminateOwnedGroup38819 in finally and verifies childESRCH. Initial5second-window/200ms version independently showed thesameownership loss and wasalsofullycleaned. No realPy/Torch/model/ledger isused."
      ],
      "impact": "The claimed wholeownedtree termination afterouterparentdeath isnotguaranteed. Reservation/lease mayremain when theouterparentdies, but theownedsubprocess canoutlive itswindow, violating thehard resource boundary and preventing safeclosure. The normalparentalivecleanup tests do notcover thisdouble-exit path. Noactualmaturepilot wasexecuted.",
